+# Snapshot identity: interning `(repo, rev)` as one id
+
+Status: PLAN ONLY. Written before implementation, per the planning protocol.
+Branch: `snapshot-identity` off `v11` (24782c3d).
+
+Three previously-separate tasks were folded into this arc: repo-scoping the
+unscoped rebuild deletes, adding a `repo` column to the rels lacking one, and
+interning `(repo, rev)`. Section 0 records where the arc's stated premises did
+not survive measurement, because two of the three tasks change shape once the
+receipts are in.
+
+---
+
+## 0. Receipts, and where the stated premises were wrong
+
+Every number below was measured on this worktree at 24782c3d.
+
+### 0.1 "~80 built-in rels carry `rev` with no `repo`" is wrong. It is 12.
+
+Full census of all 112 catalogued built-in rels (`src/engine/decls.rs` plus the
+20 `RelKind` impls under `src/rels/`):
+
+| bucket | count | rels |
+|---|---|---|
+| both `repo` and `rev` | 7 | `file`, `type_edge_rev`, `type_entity_rev`, `call_def_rev`, `df_node_repo_rev`, `const_value_rev`, `file_lines` |
+| `rev`, no `repo` | **12** | `module_import`, `module_edge_rev`, `module_unresolved_rev`, `crate_edge`, `module_binding_resolved_rev`, `module_binding_rev`, `type_link_rev`, `call_edge_rev`, `df_node_rev`, `df_arg_rev`, `df_field_rev`, `df_lit_rev` |
+| `repo`, no `rev` | 25 | `scip_want`, `rev_cmp_want`, `checkout`, `checkout_done`, `checkout_plan`, `type_edge`, `type_entity`, `doc_comment`, `doc_tag`, `call_def`, `call_site`, `df_node_repo`, `const_value`, `doc_node`, `doc_ref`, `head`, `rev_advanced`, `git_ref`, `rev_behind`, `scip_def`, `scip_ref`, `scip_edge`, `scip_occurrence`, `scip_binding`, `repo` |
+| neither | 68 | `df_node`, `df_edge`, `call_edge`, `type_link`, `module_edge`, `node`, `child`, `string`, `ref`, … |
+
+7 + 12 + 25 + 68 = 112. Verified.
+
+The consequence is that the "add a `repo` column to the 80 rels lacking it"
+sub-task does not exist as stated. The real shape is:
+
+- 12 rels genuinely need their repo half. Small, tractable.
+- **68 rels carry NEITHER coordinate.** These are the actually-unscopeable ones,
+  and no amount of `(repo, rev)` interning reaches them, because they have no
+  coordinate column to replace. This is the larger problem the arc's framing hid.
+  It is called out here rather than silently absorbed; see section 6.
+
+### 0.2 `Type::Rev` is real; `Type::Repo` is still vestigial.
+
+`Type` (`src/ast.rs:5`) is `{ Text, Int, Path, File, Dir, Repo, Rev }`.
+21 columns are typed `Type::Rev` (20 in `decls.rs` — the arc said 19, the
+undercount is `decls.rs:13`, which types both `id` and `oid` as `Type::Rev` on
+one line — plus `src/rels/filelines.rs:33`).
+
+**Zero** columns anywhere are typed `Type::Repo`. Every `repo` column in every
+built-in decl is `Type::Text`. `Type::Repo` parses (`ast.rs:23`), ranks in the
+type arena (`type_arena.rs:227`) and is accepted as a coordinate type
+(`engine/mod.rs:1268,1276`), and is used by nothing. The repo half never got the
+treatment the rev half got in a0a0ff25.
+
+### 0.3 The delete census: not ~30, about 90, and the dominant idiom is worse than unscoped.
+
+Full enumeration is in section 5. The headline correction:
+
+- Only **three** delete sites in the entire tree are repo-scoped:
+  `meta.rs:1319` (`_file`, scoped by both `repo` and `rev`),
+  `source_rows.rs:46` (`_prov`), `source_rows.rs:53` (`_where_bytes`).
+- `src/db.rs:1285`, inside `Db::reload_rel`, is `DELETE FROM {table}` with **no
+  WHERE clause at all**. It is reached through `Engine::refresh_rel`
+  (`src/engine/mod.rs:953-983`), which fans out to ~60 distinct `rel_*` tables.
+  The arc was right that a previous audit missed it; it is not merely
+  unscoped, it is the single delete that most of the engine's writes go through.
+- A second family (`derive.rs:484,510,546,1129,1544,2113,2114,2364,2477`) does
+  full-table wipes of derived rel heads, also with no WHERE.
+- A third family IS rev-scoped but repo-blind: `extract/mod.rs:695,725,1054,1120,1137`
+  and `storage/call.rs:527,769-781`. Two repos sitting on the same branch name
+  cross-contaminate here today. This is the family snapshot identity fixes
